that I don't go through bad things. This

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:15.080
is all part of life itself. Suffering is

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:17.000
a part of life, too, but sometimes we

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:19.400
have to make certain sacrifices to get

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:21.360
what we want. Other times, things happen

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:23.800
and there will always be a price to pay,

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:26.280
but there is also always a lesson to

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:28.600
learn. So, in return, we gain whatever

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:30.840
we put into that. That is the law of

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:32.720
cause and effect. It is a guarantee that

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:34.640
we will always reap what we sow. So, if

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:36.400
we manage to learn our lessons, that

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:38.760
means we will become better because of

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:41.000
it. But, the real mindset shift is if

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:43.240
you learn to listen to yourself and do

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:45.320
what you believe is right, no matter

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.400
what happens, it will all be for your

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:49.240
ultimate good. And then, if you can

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:51.240
level up that purpose, you can also be

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:53.290
generous with your energy, too, and that

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:54.600
is a beautiful thing. Now,

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:57.720
[clears throat] let's talk about my

00:21:54.600 --> 00:22:00.680
favorite word, enough, or enoughness.

00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:03.680
All of our fears and insecurity lives in

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:06.200
anticipation, but never in the present

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:09.400
moment. This is all happening in our

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:11.720
heads, which is why the word enoughness

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:13.800
is such a loaded gun. It sounds like a

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:15.520
finish line that one day you will wake

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:18.000
up and you're there and your life will

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:20.600
feel complete, but that word enough is a

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:23.480
moving goalpost. The concept of

00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:26.200
fulfillment or completion itself, even

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:28.600
in Buddhism, is essentially an empty

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:30.960
feeling. So, the more I looked outward,

00:22:28.600 --> 00:22:32.880
wondering if I'm enough or not, the

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:35.240
worse I felt about myself. Whenever I

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:37.400
can finally unplug, even when I'm on

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:39.680
this remote island, I was not thinking

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:41.720
about people on social media. I was not

00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:44.440
comparing myself to anybody. [music]

00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:47.640
I wasn't thinking about how inferior I

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:50.120
was. I was just being present and living

00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:53.120
my life and enjoying what the world has

00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:55.400
to offer. My mind becomes unhealthy the

00:22:53.120 --> 00:22:57.880
more I scroll and compare myself to

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:59.600
other people, which we're all vulnerable

00:22:57.880 --> 00:23:01.720
to. We're not meant to see into other

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:03.920
people's So, like this. This is a very

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:06.360
recent technological development, and

00:23:03.920 --> 00:23:09.480
it's not normal. It's a huge distraction

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:11.600
that keeps us exhausted, and when we're

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:13.600
exhausted all the time, we don't have

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:15.440
energy, and we're not conscious. The

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:17.320
more you scroll, the further your sense

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:19.440
of self gets because you're measuring

00:23:17.320 --> 00:23:21.920
yourself up against people who you're

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:23.600
not meant to be, and you don't know what

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:25.720
their lives actually look like. And

00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:28.320
eventually, you lose your own thoughts

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:30.640
and your sense of discernment and your

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:32.640
opinions. And that is such a huge

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:34.320
distortion. There's so many of us, we

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:36.480
don't even know how to trust ourselves

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:38.440
anymore. This is why I give myself the

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:39.720
gift of unplugging every now and then.

00:23:38.440 --> 00:23:41.960
Even if I have to go to a place that has

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:44.560
no reception, so be it. It's a blessing

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:46.320
to remove that distortion even for just

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:48.080
a few days because it makes you realize

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:50.080
things. Just to remind ourselves, you

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:52.960
know what? We're living our best life

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:54.680
that we can in this moment, and that is

00:23:52.960 --> 00:23:56.560
not just enough. It's [music]

00:23:54.680 --> 00:23:59.160
everything. Nothing is missing from my

00:23:56.560 --> 00:24:01.000
life. There is no never enough because

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:02.760
the word enough means nothing to me, and

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:04.680
you will never be a better version of

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:07.280
anybody else. You can only ever be

00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:09.400
yourself, and even yourself is

00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:11.280
